    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## What happened\n\nIn a chat session, the turn-end **Files Changed** card shows a **Review** button and individual file rows, but clicking either does nothing visible \u2014 no inspector opens with the diff, no file tab opens.\n\nReported by @goatedinsaan in [#report-bugs](https://discord.com/channels/1476302178913357958/1541396901281398794/1542179553680556202): *\"in this section I can click on 'review' and each files but nothing opens?\"*\n\n## Root cause\n\nRegression from the file-explorer refactor ([#4252](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4252)):\n\n1. `handleOpenFiles` no longer set `filesChangedOnly`, so **Review** opened the Files inspector as an empty full-tree explorer instead of the changed-files diff view \u2014 appeared to do nothing.\n2. File-row clicks passed raw turn-diff paths (basenames / relative paths) to `openCenterFile` without resolving them to workspace paths, so no center tab opened.\n3. Nested tooltip triggers on the file rows could swallow the click itself.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- **Review** \u2192 Files inspector opens on the changed-files diff list.\n- Clicking a file row \u2192 file opens in a center tab with the correct diff.\n- Path tooltip on hover shows the full worktree path.\n\n## Fix\n\nFixed by [#4563](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4563) (restores `filesChangedOnly`, adds `matchWorkspaceFilePath` resolution, moves tooltip onto the row button).\n",
